Object.assign(DIALOG_CLIPS.clips,{"tom|I got it. The library is whispering.":"","grace|Tata. TATA. Did you get my text? I sent it from Mom’s phone. She said I could. She said it after.":"","rose|A book told me Boppy eats cookies in the car. In the CAR, Tata. Before DINNER.":"","tom|...That one is true. Everybody knows that one.":"","grace|A book told everybody I sing in the shower. Which is PRIVATE. Also I am very good.":"","grace|Page says everything is fine. Page has said fine eleven times. I counted. Nobody says fine eleven times if it is fine.":"","grace|Twelve.":"","page|Oh! Tom. Girls. Welcome to the Hush Library. Everything is fine.":"","page|...It is not fine. It started a week ago. It comes up from the Stacks, downstairs. The old part.":"","tom|Books overhear things.":"","page|Books overhear EVERYTHING. That is why we whisper in here. It was never for the people. It is for the books.":"","rose|Are there monsters down there? Say yes.":"","page|The Reading Room doors use the old card catalog lock. I lost the password in 1998.":"","page|There are three sections. Fiction, Nonfiction and Picture Books. And the Reading Room, at the very back.":"","page|Then you are in charge of the signs. Here. The staff door is open.":"","grace|I have read every book in the kids section. Twice. I can read ALL the signs.":"","page|Every book down there is whispering. Everything they ever heard. Seventy years of people reading quietly and thinking nobody was listening.":"","tom|I do talk to my bread. It is part of the process.":"","page|Please be careful. And please, do not answer the books. It only encourages them.":"","rose|Tata. Tata. The books are looking at us.":"","grace|Books cannot look. They do not have... okay, that one has eyes.":"","grace|I can read every sign. Rose cannot read yet.":"","grace|FICTION is that way. NONFICTION is that way. PICTURE BOOKS are down there. The READING ROOM is at the top.":"","grace|...That is actually true.":"","tom|Somebody down here knows the password. We ask nicely. Then we ask less nicely.":"","tom|Lamby’s Big Day. Page one. Lamby woke up and decided it was going to be a big day.":"","rose|Do the voice. Do Lamby’s voice.":"","tom|(a very small voice) Today I am going to jump on everybody.":"","grace|Okay. That is actually a good book. Do not tell anyone I said that.":"","bigone|And then... the uncle walked into Fiction... and he saw... he saw...":"","tom|Saw what.":"","bigone|Find out next time!":"","grace|That is SO annoying. Finish your SENTENCES.":"","grace|Okay. Everybody up. I am in charge of getting up. Up, up, UP.":"","rose|Tata. What did you see? When you walked into Fiction?":"","grace|The first letter is circled in gold pen. S.":"","grace|That is all three cards, Tata. Card one, card two, card three. Three gold letters.":"","tom|A password for the Reading Room. In card order.":"","grump|Actually, it is li-BRAR-y. Two Rs. Everybody says it wrong. Actually.":"","tom|A green book being very dramatic.":"","grump|Actually, you said it bossy.":"","grace|Actually, I KNOW that. Actually, I said it right.":"","grace|It does NOT sound like me. Tata. Tell her.":"","tom|...Let us focus on the encyclopedia.":"","grace|Tata. Am I a know-it-all? Be honest. Actually, do not be honest.":"","rose|Tata. It sounds like Grace.":"","tom|The other one is why you are in charge of the signs down here.":"","grace|...Okay. I can work on the telling part. A little. Starting tomorrow.":"","grace|The first letter is circled in gold pen. H.":"","toad|BOO!":"","rose|AAAAH!":"","rose|...Hey. HEY. Nobody scares ME. I do the scaring. That is MY job.":"","toad|...Boo?":"","rose|BOOOOOOO!":"","grace|Rose. You scared a book.":"","rose|Tata, did you see? I scared it back. It was TERRIFIED.":"","tom|It was terrified. Best scaring I have ever seen. Ten out of ten.":"","rose|Tata. The door talked.":"","grace|It dropped a card! An old catalog card. It says CARD 3 OF 3, and the title is HUSH, LITTLE LAMBY.":"","tom|The thing behind the door talked. Stay close.":"","grace|Tata. On the dais. It is a book. A really, REALLY big book.":"","log|...Visitors. Nobody comes to the Reading Room. Nobody has come since 1952.":"","tom|You are the one whispering.":"","log|I am the oldest book in the Stacks. Seventy years on this shelf. Nobody has checked me out. Nobody has opened me. Not once.":"","log|So I listened. Everybody who ever sat in this room thought nobody could hear them. I heard ALL of it.":"","rose|You told everybody Boppy eats cookies in the car.":"","log|If nobody will read me, then I will read THEM. Out loud. To everybody.":"","grace|You cannot just tell people’s secrets! That is the rudest thing a book can do! That is a RULE!":"","log|Then read me. Go on. Nobody ever does.":"","tom|Girls, behind me. No touching, please.":"","grace|Up, everybody. I am in charge now.":"","log|...Fine. The end. I will be quiet. I am very good at quiet. I have had a lot of practice.":"","log|He does. In the CAR.":"","grace|And look. The checkout card, in the pocket. One stamp. DUE BACK 1952. No name. Just a little clock.":"","rose|Somebody took it out and did not READ it? That is so sad.":"","tom|And brought it back with a coin in it. Look at those corners. Very neat.":"","grace|Somebody DID open it, then. To put the coin in.":"","grace|I am adding it to MY list. Mine has a chart AND a key now.":"","page|Listen. It is quiet. Properly quiet. The good kind. The dictionaries are snoring.":"","grace|It just wanted somebody to read it. That is all. All of it was because nobody read it.":"","page|Then we will read it. Story time, Saturdays, out loud. And I think I know who should do the voices.":"","page|Grace. This is for you. A Gold Library Card. No limit. No late fees. Ever.":"","grace|No late fees. EVER? Tata. I am going to take out every book. Every single one. Alphabetically.":"","page|And sweaters. I knit one every winter. I have run out of people. Please take some.":"","tom|I am adding it to the list.":"","tom|\"I said yes for you. Love you. Bring the starter.\"":"","grace|Forty people? Tata. That is a FEAST.":"","tom|...Bready Mercury is going to need a bigger jar.":"","page|It is quiet. Properly quiet. The good kind. Thank you, Tom.":"","rose|It is itchy. I love it.":"","tom|A text from TNB. \"Babe. Bernadette signed you up for the 2nd Ave potluck. You are on bread. For forty people.\"":"","page|I am fine. Everything is fine. The dictionaries have not slept in a week.":"","page|It is fine. Everything is fine. Please whisper.":"","page|...Did you hear that? That was not me. I would know my own shush.":"","skeeter|Everybody uses me and then forgets which page I was on.":"","skeeter|Shh. The books are listening. They are ALWAYS listening.":"","skeeter|SHHHH! Again!":"","page|The Stacks are through the staff door. Please be careful. And please do not answer the books.":"","skeeter|Round 4. Quietly. SHHH.":"","skeeter|Round 5. Quietly. SHHH.":"","skeeter|Round 2. Quietly. SHHH.":"","skeeter|I mark your place. Nobody marks mine.":"","skeeter|...shhh. Shhhh. Shh.":"","log|I am the corner of page 212. Somebody stopped reading here in 1987.":"","log|Unfolded! Round two!":"","log|Round 2. Still creased.":"","skeeter|Round 3. Quietly. SHHH.":"","log|Round 3. Still creased.":"","log|Round 4. Still creased.":"","log|Nobody ever came back to finish. I have been folded for forty years.":"","log|Use a bookmark. That is all I ask. A BOOKMARK.":"","log|Round 5. Still creased.":"","log|...somebody folded me. Somebody always folds me.":"","bigone|Previously, on this fight...":"","bigone|Round 2. And then... and then...":"","bigone|Round 3. And then... and then...":"","bigone|Round 4. And then... and then...":"","bigone|Round 5. And then... and then...":"","bigone|Nobody ever finishes me. They read the first chapter and put me back. Every time.":"","bigone|...and then... and THEN...":"","grump|Nobody looks things up anymore. They just ask their phones. Their phones are WRONG.":"","grump|Kangaroo. Kettle. Kindness. I know them all. Nobody asks.":"","grump|Correction! Round two!":"","grump|Round 2. Footnote 2.":"","grump|Round 3. Footnote 3.":"","grump|Round 4. Footnote 4.":"","bigone|And then the uncle turned around and saw... no. I will not say.":"","grump|Round 5. Footnote 5.":"","grump|...actually. Actually. Ac-tu-al-ly.":"","grump|I am volume K. I know everything that starts with K.":"","toad|Nobody opens me anymore. I have been ready to pop for six years.":"","toad|BOO! Again!":"","toad|Round 2. Surprise!":"","toad|Round 3. Surprise!":"","toad|Round 4. Surprise!":"","toad|Round 5. Surprise!":"","toad|...boo. Boo? No? Nobody?":"","toad|I am supposed to be the surprise.":"","bigone|Find out next time. Same shelf. Same book.":"","toad|Kids open me and scream. Then they laugh. Then they open me again. I love it.":"","log|Seventy years on this shelf. Nobody has opened me once.":"","log|You hear things, when nobody reads you. You hear EVERYTHING.":"","log|Chapter two. Again.":"","log|Round 4. Page 4.":"","log|Round 5. Page 5.":"","log|Round 3. Page 3.":"","log|I know what you whispered. I know what everybody whispered.":"","amy|Report cards. Thirty of them. Take the girls. They both have library cards. I made sure.":"","deedee|Not today, honey. Book club at four. We are reading the same book as last month. Nobody finished it.":"","log|Round 2. Page 2.":"","sal|Airport? You just got here. Your niece called the depot. From her mother’s phone.":"","boppy|A library? I read a book once. 1974. It was about fish. It was not accurate.":"","sal|She said, and I quote, \"tell Tata the library is being WEIRD.\" She hung up before I could ask how.":"","log|...nobody. Not once. Since 1952.":"","rose|THAT IS WHAT I DO.":"","rose|I can read PICTURES. Pictures are harder.":"","grace|Not a little bit. ALL the books. At the same time. And they are saying THINGS.":"","grace|It dropped a card! An old catalog card. It says CARD 1 OF 3, and the title is SECRETS OF THE SOUP DUMPLING.":"","tom|You know a lot. And you tell people. Those are two different things, and only one of them needs a little work.":"","toad|AAAAH!":"","grace|It dropped a card! An old catalog card. It says CARD 2 OF 3, and the title is HOW TO WHISPER, VOLUME 2.":"","tom|A gold coin. Same little clock face.":"","grace|Tata, something fell out of it. Something gold. It was being used as a bookmark.":"","grace|Tata, it TELLS us its chapter. Mystery, Chatter. Adventure, Kinetic. Read the message. And maybe somebody should just read it. Out loud. Three times.":"","page|Story time is Saturdays now. The Unread asked for Grace. By name.":"","tom|The sundial. The steamer. The sign-up sheet. My jar. Now a book nobody has opened since 1952.":""});
